{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"b36bbfc54805cde8","type":"text","text":"[[Yormindar.canvas]]\n#Volstarian_Dynasty ","x":-560,"y":-320,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"cc528371ab654f74","x":-560,"y":-200,"width":1760,"height":840,"type":"text","text":"Residuum mines:\n\nThe Bottom most part of Yormindar, anything passed this floor is unmapped and not owned by the city. Because below this floor is the underdark.\n\n\n\n\nNevia says don’t make it safe so add roaming Loth sworn Drow\n\n\nIf a spell is cast the caster must roll a d20:\n\nIf they roll a 4-10 they roll a d6 with the following potential disasters.\n\t1. You blink into the Astral sea until the end of your next turn.\n\t2. The spell fails.\n\t3. Nothing happens.\n\t4. Your hands begin to glow a bright green within 30 feet of you.\n\t5. Illusory butterflies appear around the caster.\n\t6. The caster speaks only in deep-speech for 1 hour.\n\nOn an 11-16 roll a d6 for the following effects:\n\t1. Polymorph into a bat.\n\t2. A double cast but at yourself.\n\t3. A soft jazz begins to play from the targeted spell location.\n\t4. You gain immunity to the condition or element of your spell casted.\n\t5. You begin to violently vomit pink rainbows for 1 minute making a dc 16 Con save at the beginning of every turn if in combat.\n\t6. You cast fire ball at your feet.\n\nOn a 1 You turn into a potted plant see wild magic table \n--\nOn a 2 You spend two spell slots of that level if you don’t have one you take 1 d6 force damage per spell slot level\n--\nOn a 3 Your spell fails and you hear a sad trombone playing\n--\n17 - 18 Nothing happens.\n--\nOn a 19 roll a d100 on a 95 or higher a card from the deck of many things appears in your palm but doesn’t activate until you look at it.\n--\nOn a 20 You don’t expend the spell slot.\n\n"},
		{"id":"68c4280c4149dcee","x":-560,"y":720,"width":743,"height":332,"type":"text","text":"The Refinery:\n\nIt is a three day walk through the refinery location to the end of the mines. \n\nGreen Residuum is scattered all throughout this area and is shinning like Christmas ornaments, all throughout the air there are green orbs that look like fireflies.\n\nA scattering of minecarts tipped over or not, pickaxes and other mining equipment.\n\nThere is an outpost here a large cabin of sorts, Inside is a hall with tables and chairs and bunk beds all across the walls. This is where the miners would relax and sleep as they spent multiple days at a time down here sometimes even weeks.  \n"},
		{"id":"382e1676faeb5b43","x":-640,"y":1520,"width":1105,"height":526,"type":"text","text":"The puzzle:\n\nThe door Is a giagantic metallic wall made of obsidian rock and iron.\n\n\nAt the foot of the door is a circular vortex of sorts that falls into a ball shaped whole in the middle.\n\nOn the wall there is an image of a Giant lifiting a massive rock and slamming it down into the ground.\n\nAlong the floor is a trail of foot prints that lead toward the magma fall.\n\nHidden on the far left side of the magma fall there are 24 buttons and a letter above each one and on a plaque the words. \"only those who know the name of our Father of creation shall pass the wall of fire\"\n\nThe key is the word Moradin (Xandar knows it)\n\nAlong the wall is the story of the God of creation.\n\nImages of a Anvil striking the grounds enriching it with minerals and creating a massive mountain that is now known as Yormindar.\n\nBehind the magma fall lies the dragon.\n\nJust at the entrance is a sphere made of pure residuum and upon bringing it to the foot of the door it will open.\n"},
		{"id":"539038b0206fbf88","x":215,"y":720,"width":865,"height":440,"type":"text","text":"The Endless Abyss: \n\nAt the very end of the mines lies a ravine hundreds of feet across and deep. At the bottom of the ravine is a flowing river of magma. To the left a magma fall. All the cavern walls are lined with residuum and glowing red rocks.\n\nAt the very bottom sleeps a red dragon who is mostly friendly to whoever is unfortunate enough to encounter him Rythar is not angry by default but is quick to piss off. His layer is located at the bottom behind the magma fall. \n\nFar down and to the right lies the EmberHold entrance at the end of a long cave walk spanning 2 days. \n\nOn the farside of the ravine there is a drow who broke free of the eternal tourment of Lolth and seeks a way out of the mines his name is Xandar.\n\nXandar is located on the far side (at any point) behind a thin sheet of residuum and will be visible with a high enough  perception check.\n\n\nOn the entrance side there is a not very safe walkway down the ravine side that will eventually bring them down to the bottom, the big issue is there are is a door blocking the path that leads to the EmberHold.\n"},
		{"id":"df2afb125d46d2e1","x":560,"y":1560,"width":760,"height":320,"type":"text","text":"Behind the Magma fall: \n\nBehind the Magma fall Rythar sleeps.\n\nBeyond the initial threshold where the residuum sphere is.\n\nRythars layer is a giant dome like cavern with magma falling from the ceiling and a scattering of residuum behind him. The dome is lit only by the magma and the cavern is about 200 feet in diameter.\n\nRythar is once again not aggressive unless provoked but he will not be willing to lend a hand in anyway and if the party talks with him he will not give them any helpful information.\n"}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"1364db728c08f36a","fromNode":"539038b0206fbf88","fromSide":"right","toNode":"df2afb125d46d2e1","toSide":"right"},
